    <DataNode elementId="FLAVANONES" textLabel="a flavanone" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="10251" dataSource="PubChem-compound" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="400" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">Flavanones are |FRAME: Flavanoids flavans| with a keto group at position 4. They are similar to |FRAME: Flavones| but lack the double bond between carbons 2 and 3. Thus, while |FRAME: CPD-8485| is 2-phenylchromen-4-one, |FRAME: CPD-2043 flavanone| is 2,3-dihydro-2-phenylchromen-4-one.</Comment>
